comments.body:
@Nitsuh Abebe

When our now-grown children were little, they came up with names for foods that have stuck over the years: noo-noos from my son (who loved noodles aka plain pasta) and snake from my daughter (who got upset when my husband announced one day that we were splurging for dinner and having steak; she thought he said snake). Today my husband and I (empty nesters now) both call tofu, toad food.

Within my extended family, especially among my siblings, we still jokingly use words our mom and other relatives (all long gone now) would say. Our favorite is "piddle" from our mom, for anything she thought was silly or stupid.

@Emily Baumgaertner Nunn     

For me, it's neuroticism. 

Or maybe not. I can't really be sure . . .
